 {"question":6,"answer":"MAJOR: a finite row k0=1e20 squares to Inf in fp32. Norm Inf gives unit0 and code8; q=-ones yields coefficient -0.0803470984 and packed score -Inf. Dense reconstruction has 31 +Inf and 33 -Inf coordinates, hence NaN dot. Packed softmax weights [1,0,1] and denominator2 are finite; dense NaN accumulator times its guarded zero remains NaN. Thus it can hide a dense non-finite row. This does not demonstrate a new F-to-F2 finite result change: both retain the same overflow path. No claim of general finite-output parity with dense is made.","evidence":"BLIND_CHECKS.json; D12_SOFTMAX.json; quant.py:122-127; packed.cuh:94-112,198-201; apa_sp1_1.cuh:73-102; staged r01, CPU prefix PASS"},
